# HypeProof Studio — let ONE webview request the microphone: our extension's chat view.
#
# v4. FIVE HUNKS ACROSS THREE FILES. Read the version history before editing; each
# version fixed a real, measured failure and the third one was mine to own.
#
#   v1  edited inside the inline script, left its CSP hash alone
#         -> Chromium refused the script, chat and start pages came up BLANK,
#            with build success, verify-branding pass and a normal artifact.
#   v2  fixed the hash. Screens rendered, microphone still DENIED.
#         -> measured chain (run 34623231942, real Mac):
#              top workbench document        allowed = TRUE
#              outer workbench -> webview    allow had no microphone
#              webview shell document        FALSE, allowlist []
#              inner shell -> content        allow HAD microphone;   (v2's hunk)
#              chat content document         FALSE, allowlist []
#              getUserMedia                  NotAllowedError
#            Permissions Policy is delegated per level, so an inner allow cannot
#            re-grant what the embedder never received. v2 patched one level too deep.
#   v3  added the OUTER delegation, keyed on the owning extension id. IT WORKS:
#         run 34631073535, real Mac -> outcome=granted, trackCount=1,
#         trackReadyState=live, shell and content allowsFeature('microphone') true.
#         BUT the scope claim in its header was WRONG. It said the preview surface
#         was out of scope "by construction" because hypeproof-preview is a separate
#         sprint. Today the preview webview is created INSIDE hypeproof-chat
#         (previewProvider.ts:127, enableScripts: true), so it shares the extension
#         id and v3 admitted it. Confirmed by measurement, not argument: the
#         same-extension START PAGE also reported microphone policy true.
#   v4  ANDs a second discriminator so the surface is one webview, not three.
#
# THE SURFACE. hypeproof-chat owns three script-enabled webviews:
#
#   chatPanelProvider.ts:562   chat        webview VIEW    <- voice lives here only
#   startPage.ts:50            start page  webview panel
#   previewProvider.ts:127     preview     webview panel
#
# v3 delegated to all three. v4 delegates to the chat view alone:
#
#   outer  webviewElement.ts   extension id AND options.purpose === 'webviewView'
#   inner  pre/index.html      the same two values from the shell's query string
#
# Neither discriminator is guessed. `WebviewOptions.purpose` is declared at
# webview.ts:97 in the pinned upstream (`WebviewContentPurpose.WebviewView =
# 'webviewView'`) and is passed straight into `_createElement(options, …)`;
# `_initElement` copies it into the shell's query string (`if (options.purpose)
# params.purpose = options.purpose`), and the shipped artifact's captured iframe src
# carries `purpose=webviewView` on the chat frame and omits it on the start page. A
# const enum compiles to the bare string, so the literal comparison needs no import.
#
# Residual, stated plainly: an extension declaring the same publisher.name would
# collide with the built-in, and any future webview VIEW added to this extension
# would inherit the delegation. This is strictly narrower than v3, not a capability
# boundary. Whether the chat view may request the microphone at all is a human
# decision (H-08), not something this patch settles.
#
# THE CSP HASH. `pre/index.html` carries the SHA-256 of its own inline script inside
# its own CSP meta. Hunks 2 and 3 edit inside that script, so the hash moves again:
#   stock sha256-TaWGDzV7c9rUH2q/5ygOyYUHSyHIqBMYfucPh3lnKvU=
#   v2    sha256-F3cWHVJseSLSGcewJCgf4+lHqww+TPBT0lgjBiFyf7c=
#   v3    sha256-VQFZcn+4j5AR46C+MNBJ98l02nDWSQrtwWw+V6mBZmc=
#   v4    sha256-QcHyzmP/gRJ3S2FZ9OKJAeMmN/qUuumD37tL4bNuyMc=
#
# Not guessed: the method reproduces the stock hash from the unmodified file before
# computing anything, and the consuming repo's own gate
# (scripts/check-webview-csp-hash.py — a separate code path) agrees with the value on
# the patched source.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: compute the hash from the script AFTER the hunk 2 and 3 edits, then
# write it into the CSP meta. The meta sits outside the script element so writing it
# does not perturb the hash — asserted while generating this patch.
#
# ANY future edit inside that script invalidates this hash, and the symptom is a
# blank webview with no visible cause. verify-branding.sh check 11 makes that a build
# failure instead of a silent ship.
#
# NOT CLAIMED: audible output. Capture is verified; playback is still web-audio-only.
# H-04 (a human granting the OS prompt after a delay) is NOT RUN — the 222ms resolve
# observed on v3 is not a delayed-permission test.
#
# Generated from microsoft/vscode at 560a9dba96f9 (upstream/stable.json tag 1.116.0).
